Support CMakeUserPresets.json for persistent build configuration

The PyTorch build system now reads CMakeUserPresets.json from the repo
root during cmake configuration. This allows users to persistently set
cache variables (like USE_ROCM, USE_CUDA) and environment variables
(like ROCM_PATH, PYTORCH_ROCM_ARCH) without needing to export env vars
each session. Real environment variables still take precedence over
preset values.

Also fixes ninja detection to re-evaluate after preset environment
variables are loaded.

